{"status":"answered","explanation":"The evidence indicates Pliny requested an architect or someone skilled in waterworks construction because the previous attempts to build the aqueduct in Nicomedia had failed, and he believed a skilled person would be necessary to ensure the new design would succeed. Trajan required Pliny to examine the misconduct regarding the large sums spent on the aqueduct and to ensure the city was supplied with water.","claims":[{"text":"Pliny requested an architect or someone skilled in waterworks construction because the previous attempts to build the aqueduct in Nicomedia had failed, and he believed a skilled person would be necessary to ensure the new design would succeed.","citations":[{"id":"pliny:XLVI:1","path":"vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0157","quote":"But that this work may not meet with the same ill-success as the former, it will be necessary to send here an architect, or some one skilled in the construction of this kind of waterworks."}
]
},{"text":"Trajan required Pliny to examine the misconduct regarding the large sums spent on the aqueduct and to ensure the city was supplied with water.","citations":[{"id":"pliny:XLVII:1","path":"vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0158","quote":"But really it is no less incumbent upon you to examine by whose misconduct it has happened that such large sums have been thrown away upon this, lest they apply the money to private purposes, and the aqueduct in question, like the preceding, should be begun, and afterwards left unfinished."}
]
}]}

